    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy notice</string>
    <string name="privacy_body">• Ad blocking is a local VPN that works only on your device. Regular internet traffic does not pass through it; only DNS requests are filtered on-device and then sent to the DNS server you chose.\n• DNS block logs and scan history are stored only on your device and deleted automatically after the retention period.\n• Your installed-app list, DNS logs and APK files are never sent to any server.\n• Updates only download filter lists and the threat DB; the threat DB is applied only after its Ed25519 signature is verified.\n• The QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES permission is used only to scan installed apps for malware.\n• Contact: pm999@naver.com</string>
    <string name="onb1_title">Blocks ads, trackers and phishing sites</string>
    <string name="onb1_body">A local VPN that runs only on your device filters DNS requests. Regular traffic does not go through it, so browsing stays fast and your data never goes to our servers. Android will ask you to allow the VPN connection when you turn it on.</string>
    <string name="onb2_title">Scans for malware and shows the evidence</string>
    <string name="onb2_body">Uses a SHA-256 malware hash DB, YARA-X patterns, static APK analysis and risky-permission analysis together. Every result shows which engine decided and why. App code is never executed.</string>
    <string name="onb3_title">Minimal personal data</string>
    <string name="onb3_body">Your app list, DNS logs and APK files never leave the device. Logs are deleted automatically after the period you set. The \'query installed apps\' permission is used to scan installed apps.</string>
